\section{Evaluation}
We deployed the protocol on two hundred nodes distributed over an agricultural field. Table~1 lists the configurations. Convergence was measured as the number of rounds needed until all estimates were within one percent of the true average. Across all configurations, the adaptive protocol converged within the theoretical bound while transmitting substantially fewer messages than the baseline.

